      "message": "The flag is enabled on every `JDK \u003e\u003d 25`, not only JDK 25, as the commit message says.\nFor example, this would enable it even if Gerrit was already running on JDK 27 already, which, as you mention, enables compact object headers by default so it would be redundant.\n\nDid you mean to enable it _only_ for JDK 25?\n\n```\nif (Runtime.version().feature() !\u003d 25) {\n  return;\n}\n```\n\nIf JDK 26 also requires Gerrit to enable it, we should document it accordingly.",
